From 0ba048943b1f15cef0fead1706552475da209339 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Praveen <113331169+praveen9161@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 12:22:03 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Publish GPUFit workload scores as device attributes

Add an opt-in --gpufit-scores-configmap flag (GPUFIT_SCORES_CONFIGMAP) to
the kubelet plugin. When set, the driver polls that ConfigMap in its own
namespace every 5s and, when scores.json changes, republishes its
ResourceSlices with gpufit.io/<workload>Score int attributes, e.g.
gpufit.io/trainingScore. Claims can then select devices with CEL:

  device.attributes["gpufit.io"].trainingScore >= 80

Deleting the ConfigMap republishes the devices without scores. Scores are
validated (0-100, workload names must form valid attribute names) before
anything is published.

Helm: new value kubeletPlugin.gpufitScoresConfigMap (default "", disabled)
plus a Role/RoleBinding granting get on that one ConfigMap only.

